# columns: go trig hold
# samples: go trig hold, code nent nhold tv
# states A B C; code A=1 B=2 C=3
# first run: entry into A (code 1)
1 0 0
# A -> B: nent 1, tv 0
1 1 0
# B, hold: the internal on runs (nhold 1); the timer runs on (1 ms)
1 1 1
# hold and !trig: the internal on is the match, B -> A waits (nhold 2,
# 2 ms); on_enter does not run again (nent 1)
1 0 1
# 3 ms: the timeout is due, but held back too (nhold 3)
1 0 1
# hold released at 4 ms: on (!trig) is false, the overdue timeout fires
# at once: B -> C, tv 0
1 1 0
# C -> A
1 0 0
# A -> B: nent 2
1 1 0
# B, 1 ms
1 1 0
# disabled: the internal on does not run though hold is set (nhold 3),
# timer frozen
0 1 1
# enabled again: 2 ms, B -> A
1 0 0
